        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d8369a13-2e71-5756-803e-596553b39104",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Clothes for a Summer Hotel\n- People: Tennessee Williams, F. Scott Fitzgerald, Zelda Fitzgerald, Geraldine Page\n- Awards: Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Tennessee Williams began work on Clothes for a Summer Hotel as a \"long play\" about F. Scott Fitzgerald and Zelda Fitzgerald, and he later cut it down.\n- From the start of Clothes for a Summer Hotel, Tennessee Williams had Geraldine Page in mind to play Zelda Fitzgerald.\n- In 1980, Clothes for a Summer Hotel was a play by Tennessee Williams about the relationship between novelist F. Scott Fitzgerald and his wife Zelda Fitzgerald.\n- Geraldine Page received Academy Award nominations for Hondo (1953), Summer and Smoke (1961), Sweet Bird of Youth (1962), You're a Big Boy Now (1966), Pete 'n' Tillie (1972), Interiors (1978), and The Pope of Greenwich Village (1984).\n- In 1985, Geraldine Page won the Academy Award for Best Actress for playing Carrie Watts in The Trip to Bountiful.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8ccaab63-8a79-55ec-9d3b-14d90e84e521",
        "text": "Page: Clothes for a Summer Hotel. Sentence: Clothes for a Summer Hotel is a 1980 play by Tennessee Williams about the relationship between novelist F. Scott Fitzgerald and his wife Zelda.\nPage: Clothes for a Summer Hotel. Sentence: Williams began work in 1976 on what he envisioned as a \"long play\" about the Fitzgeralds (he eventually cut it down), and had Geraldine Page in mind to play Zelda from the start.\nPage: Geraldine Page. Sentence: An eight-time Academy Award nominee, she was nominated for \"Hondo\" (1953), \"Summer and Smoke\" (1961), \"Sweet Bird of Youth\" (1962), \"You're a Big Boy Now\" (1966), \"Pete 'n' Tillie\" (1972), \"Interiors\" (1978) and \"The Pope of Greenwich Village\" (1984), before winning the Academy Award for Best Actress for her performance as Carrie Watts in \"The Trip to Bountiful\" (1985).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
